290a|n|A turning point; the principal or highest point; top; summit; crown; apex. ; The top, or crown, of the head. ; The zenith, or the point of the heavens directly overhead. ; The point in any figure opposite to, and farthest from, the base; the terminating point of some particular line or lines in a figure or a curve; the top, or the point opposite the base.	n:17r3,93,4~17r3,93,4	N:jcp,89,5~jcp,89,5
